  [allowed] probes/lib/omsx_repl.py:382: 3-line listing (edb676f694b2) — C-BIOS, not a proprietary reference ROM: allowed-sources.md grades C-BIOS source B/Conditional — a peer clean-room reimplementation under BSD-2 whose source this project already patches (cbios-repack/), and NOT the reference implementation zerobas reimplements. The run is 3 instructions of the keyboard-buffer path, in a docstring explaining the D-LATCH2 injection window (docs/spec-probe-latch2.md §5.5); the same docstring is explicit about the line it stays on ("locating chget in the reference needs a disassembly this project does not do"). Probe source, not shipped ROM source. Flagged for the human paper trail 2026-08-06 (D-DOCJUDGE §2.6) — a judgement docs/clean-room-audit.md reserves for a human, which is why it is written down here rather than decided by the tool.
